{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_47704","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Ammoniumsalz","Ammoniumsalze","ammonium salt","ammonium salts"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_47704","description":[],"label":"ammonium salt","obo_id":"CHEBI:47704","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35273","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["quaternary ammonium compound","quaternary ammonium compounds","quaternary ammonium salt","quaternary ammonium salts"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_35273","description":["Derivatives of ammonium compounds, (NH\u003csmall\u003e\u003csub\u003e4\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/small\u003e\u003csmall\u003e\u003csup\u003e+\u003c/small\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e)Y\u003csmall\u003e\u003csup\u003e−\u003c/small\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e, in which all four of the hydrogens bonded to nitrogen have been replaced with univalent (usually organyl) groups."],"label":"quaternary ammonium salt","obo_id":"CHEBI:35273","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["quaternary ammonium compounds"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_143100","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["organic ammonium salts"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_143100","description":["Any organic salt in which the cation is ammonium"],"label":"organic ammonium salt","obo_id":"CHEBI:143100","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_147406","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["inorganic ammonium salts"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_147406","description":[],"label":"inorganic ammonium salt","obo_id":"CHEBI:147406","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_188326","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["3-methylbutanoic acid ammonium salt","FEMA 2054","ammonium 3-methylbutanoate","ammonium 3-methylbutyrate","azanium 3-methylbutanoate","isovaleric acid ammonium salt","isovaleric acid, ammonium salt"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_188326","description":["An organic ammonium salt of isovaleric acid."],"label":"ammonium isovalerate","obo_id":"CHEBI:188326","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium 3-methylbutanoate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_231858","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["NH4SCN","ammonium rhodanide","ammonium thiocyanate","thiocyanic acid ammonium salt (1:1)","thiocyanic acid ammonium salt","thiocyanic acid, ammonium salt (1:1)"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_231858","description":["The organic ammonium salt of thiocyanic acid."],"label":"ammonium thiocyanate","obo_id":"CHEBI:231858","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium thiocyanate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63050","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Formic acid, ammonium salt (1:1)","Formic acid, ammonium salt","ammonium formate","ammonium formiate","azanium formate","formic acid ammonium salt"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_63050","description":["The ammonium salt of formic acid."],"label":"ammonium formate","obo_id":"CHEBI:63050","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium formate","azanium formate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_142832","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["2,3,6-trichlorobenzeneacetic acid ammonium salt","2,3,6-trichlorophenylacetic acid, ammonium salt","ammonium (2,3,6-trichlorophenyl)acetate","ammonium 2,3,6-trichlorobenzeneacetate","ammonium chlorfenac"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_142832","description":["An ammonium salt comprising equimolar amounts of chlorfenac(1-) anions and ammonium cations. An obsolete herbicide."],"label":"chlorfenac-ammonium","obo_id":"CHEBI:142832","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium (2,3,6-trichlorophenyl)acetate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_183171","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["azanium;[(2R)-3-heptadecanoyloxy-2-[(Z)-tetradec-9-enoyl]oxypropyl] [(5R)-2,3,4,5,6-pentahydroxycyclohexyl] phosphate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_183171","description":[],"label":"1-heptadecanoyl-2-(9Z-tetradecenoyl)-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1\u0027-myo-inositol)(ammonium salt)","obo_id":"CHEBI:183171","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["azanium;[(2R)-3-heptadecanoyloxy-2-[(Z)-tetradec-9-enoyl]oxypropyl] [(5R)-2,3,4,5,6-pentahydroxycyclohexyl] phosphate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_229630","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Baker\u0027s ammonia","E503","bis(ammonium) carbonate","carbonic acid ammonium salt (1:2)","carbonic acid diammonium salt","carbonic acid, ammonium salt (1:2)","carbonic acid, diammonium salt","diammonium carbonate","hartshorn","salt of hartshorn"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_229630","description":["An ammonium salt that is the diammonium salt of carbonic acid."],"label":"ammonium carbonate","obo_id":"CHEBI:229630","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["diammonium carbonate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63038","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Ammonium nitricum","Ammonium saltpeter","Ammonium(I) nitrate (1:1)","Nitrate d\u0027ammonium","Nitrate of ammonia","Nitrato amonico","Nitric acid ammonium salt (1:1)","Nitric acid, ammonium salt","Norway saltpeter","ammonium nitrate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_63038","description":["The ammonium salt of nitric acid."],"label":"ammonium nitrate","obo_id":"CHEBI:63038","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium nitrate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_87398","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Ammonium aurintricarboxylate","Aurintricarboxylic acid ammonium salt","Aurintricarboxylic acid triammonium salt","C.I. 43810","C.I. Mordant Violet 39, triammonium salt","Triammonium 5,5\u0027-(3-carboxylato-4-oxocyclohexa-2,5-dienylidenemethylene)disalicylate","Triammonium aurintricarboxylate","mordant violet 39","trisammonium 3,3\u0027-[(3-carboxylato-4-oxocyclohexa-2,5-dien-1-ylidene)methylene]bis(6-hydroxybenzoate)"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_87398","description":["An ammonium salt that is the ammonium salt of 3,3\u0027-[(3-carboxy-4-oxocyclohexa-2,5-dien-1-ylidene)methylene]bis(6-hydroxybenzoic acid). A dye commonly used to detect the presence of the aluminium ion in an aqueous solution."],"label":"aluminon","obo_id":"CHEBI:87398","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["trisammonium 3,3\u0027-[(3-carboxylato-4-oxocyclohexa-2,5-dien-1-ylidene)methylene]bis(6-hydroxybenzoate)"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_147408","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["AP 422","AP 462","APP 422","APP","Albaplas AP 95","Amgard CL","Amgard MC","Amgard TR","Antiblaze MC","Antiblaze MCM","Budit 3076","Budit 3076DC","Budit 3077","Budit 365","DFP-I","Exolit 263","Exolit 422","Exolit 442","Exolit 454","Exolit 455","Exolit 462","Exolit 470","Exolit AP 422","Exolit AP 423","Exolit AP 462","FR-Cros 480","FR-Cros 484","Fire-Trol LCG-R","Flameguard PT 8","Hostaflam 423","Hostaflam AP 420","Hostaflam AP 422","Hostaflam AP 462","Hostaflam AP 464","Hostaflam TP-AP 751","Hostaflam TP-AP 752","Novawhite","Phos-Chek P 30","Phos-Chek P 40","Phos-Chek P 60","Poly-N 10-34-0","Poly-N 11-37-0","Sumisafe","Taien A","Taien H","ammonium polyphosphate","polyphosphoric acid ammonium salt"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_147408","description":["An inorganic ammonium salt of polyphosphate. It is used as a flame retardant and as a fertilizer. The chain length (n) of this polymer is variable and can be linear or branched."],"label":"ammonium polyphosphate","obo_id":"CHEBI:147408","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_156555","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Ammonium mercaptoacetate","Mercaptoacetic acid, monoammonium salt","Thioglycolic acid ammonium salt","ammonium sulfanylacetate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_156555","description":["An organic ammonium salt having thioglycolate(1−) as the counterion. Also known as perm salt, it has use in perming hair."],"label":"ammonium thioglycolate","obo_id":"CHEBI:156555","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium sulfanylacetate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_62947","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["AcONH4","CH3CO2NH4","CH3COONH4","E 264","E-264","E264","INS No. 264","NH4OAc","acetic acid, ammonium salt","ammonium acetate","ammonium ethanoate","azanium acetate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_62947","description":["An ammonium salt obtained by reaction of ammonia with acetic acid. A deliquescent white crystalline solid, it has a relatively low melting point (114°C) for a salt. Used as a food acidity regulator, although no longer approved for this purpose in the EU."],"label":"ammonium acetate","obo_id":"CHEBI:62947","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium acetate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_147370","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Image","Scepter","Tone-Up","ammonium 2-[(RS)-4-isopropyl-4-methyl-5-oxo-2-imidazolin-2-yl]quinoline-3-carboxylate","ammonium imazaquin","ammonium salt of (RS)-2-(4-isopropyl-4-methyl-5-oxo-2-imidazolin-2-yl)quinoline-3-carboxylate","ammonium-imazaquin","imazaquin ammonium","imazaquin monoammonium salt","rac-3-(4,5-dihydro-4-methyl-4-(1-methylethyl)-5-oxo-1H-imidazol-2-yl)-3-quinolinecarboxylic acid monoammonium salt","rac-ammonium 2-[4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]quinoline-3-carboxylate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_147370","description":["A racemate comprising equimolar amounts of (\u003ci\u003eR\u003c/i\u003e)- and (\u003ci\u003eS\u003c/i\u003e)-imazaquin-ammonium. It is a imidazolinone herbicide developed by American Cyanamid Company and is effective against perennial and annual weeds. It was registered for soybean use in 1986, and for turf use in 1987 by the trade names of \u0027Scepter\u0027 and \u0027Image\u0027 respectively."],"label":"imazaquin-ammonium","obo_id":"CHEBI:147370","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["rac-ammonium 2-[4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]quinoline-3-carboxylate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_62946","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["(NH4)2SO4","ammonium sulfate (2:1)","ammonium sulphate","diammonium sulfate","diazanium sulfate","mascagnite","sulfuric acid ammonium salt (1:2)","sulfuric acid, diammonium salt","sulphate of ammonia"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_62946","description":["An inorganic sulfate salt obtained by reaction of sulfuric acid with two equivalents of ammonia. A high-melting (decomposes above 280°C) white solid which is very soluble in water (70.6 g/100 g water at 0°C; 103.8 g/100 g water at 100°C), it is widely used as a fertilizer for alkaline soils."],"label":"ammonium sulfate","obo_id":"CHEBI:62946","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["diazanium sulfate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63037","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["2-Hydroxy-1,2,3-propanetricarboxylic acid triammonium salt","2-hydroxy-1,2,3-propanetricarboxylic acid, ammonium salt (1:3)","Ammonium citrate (3:1)","ammonium citrate tribasic","citric acid triammonium salt","tri(azaniumyl) 2-hydroxypropane-1,2,3-tricarboxylate","triammonium 2-hydroxypropane-1,2,3-tricarboxylate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_63037","description":["A citrate salt in which all three carboxy groups are deprotonated and associated with ammonium ions as counter-cations."],"label":"triammonium citrate","obo_id":"CHEBI:63037","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["tri(azaniumyl) 2-hydroxypropane-1,2,3-tricarboxylate","triammonium 2-hydroxypropane-1,2,3-tricarboxylate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63075","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["(R)-2,3-Dihydroxybutanedioic acid diammonium salt","Ammonium d-tartrate","Diammonium L-(+)-tartrate","L-(+)-tartaric acid diammonium salt","L-Tartaric acid, ammonium salt","ammonium tartrate dibasic","diammonium (2R,3R)-2,3-dihydroxysuccinate","diammonium tartrate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_63075","description":["An organic salt that is the diammonium salt of \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-(+)-tartaric acid."],"label":"diammonium L-tartrate","obo_id":"CHEBI:63075","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["diammonium (2R,3R)-2,3-dihydroxysuccinate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_751722","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Ammonium mandelate","Mandelic acid ammonium salt"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_751722","description":[],"label":"ammonium mandelate","obo_id":"CHEBI:751722","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_133230","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["ammonium 2-[(4R)-4-isopropyl-4-methyl-5-oxo-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]-5-(methoxymethyl)nicotinate","ammonium 5-(methoxymethyl)-2-[(4R)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]pyridine-3-carboxylate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_133230","description":["An ammonium salt resulting from the formal reaction of the carboxy group of (\u003ci\u003eR\u003c/i\u003e)-imazamox with 1 mol eq. of ammonia."],"label":"(R)-imazamox-ammonium","obo_id":"CHEBI:133230","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium 5-(methoxymethyl)-2-[(4R)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]pyridine-3-carboxylate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_133231","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["ammonium 2-[(4S)-4-isopropyl-4-methyl-5-oxo-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]-5-(methoxymethyl)nicotinate","ammonium 5-(methoxymethyl)-2-[(4S)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]pyridine-3-carboxylate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_133231","description":["An ammonium salt resulting from the formal reaction of the carboxy group of (\u003ci\u003eS\u003c/i\u003e)-imazamox with 1 mol eq. of ammonia."],"label":"(S)-imazamox-ammonium","obo_id":"CHEBI:133231","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium 5-(methoxymethyl)-2-[(4S)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]pyridine-3-carboxylate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_133341","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["(2-Hydroxyethyl)trimethylammonium chloride","(beta-Hydroxyethyl)trimethylammonium chloride","2-Hydroxy-N,N,N,-trimethylethanaminium chloride","2-hydroxy-N,N,N-trimethylethanaminium chloride","Bilineurin chloride","Biocolina","Biocoline","Chloride de choline","Chlorure de choline","Choline chlorhydrate","Choline hydrochloride","Cholini chloridum","Cholinium chloride","Cloruro de colina","FEMA NO. 4500","Hepacholine","Lipotril","Luridin chloride","NSC-402838","Paresan","Trimethyl(2-hydroxyethyl)ammonium chloride","choline chloride"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_133341","description":["A quaternary ammonium salt with choline cation and chloride anion."],"label":"choline chloride","obo_id":"CHEBI:133341","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["2-hydroxy-N,N,N-trimethylethanaminium chloride"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_142860","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["(2S)-2-amino-4-(hydroxymethylphosphinyl)butanoic acid monoammonium salt","ammonium (2S)-2-amino-4-(methylphosphinato)butyric acid","ammonium (2S)-2-azaniumyl-4-(methylphosphinato)butanoate","ammonium [(3S)-3-amino-3-carboxypropyl]methylphosphinate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_142860","description":["An ammonium salt resulting from the formal reaction of equimolar amounts of glufosinate-P and ammonia. A glutamine synthetase inhibitor, used as a herbicide to control annual weeds and grasses."],"label":"glufosinate-P-ammonium","obo_id":"CHEBI:142860","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium (2S)-2-amino-4-(methylphosphinato)butyric acid","ammonium (2S)-2-azaniumyl-4-(methylphosphinato)butanoate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_145558","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["(2-hydroxyethyl)trimethylammonium (2,4-dichlorophenoxy)acetate","2,4-D choline salt","2-hydroxy-N,N,N-trimethylethan-1-aminium (2,4-dichlorophenoxy)acetate","2-hydroxy-N,N,N-trimethylethanaminium (2,4-dichlorophenoxy)acetate","Enlist Duo"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_145558","description":["A quaternary ammonium salt resulting from the reaction of 2,4-D with choline. It is a post-emergence herbicide used for selective control of broadleaf weeds."],"label":"2,4-D choline","obo_id":"CHEBI:145558","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["2-hydroxy-N,N,N-trimethylethanaminium (2,4-dichlorophenoxy)acetate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_147371","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["ammonium 2-[(4R)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]quinoline-3-carboxylate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_147371","description":["An ammonium salt resulting from the formal reaction of the carboxy group of (\u003ci\u003eR\u003c/i\u003e)-imazaquin with 1 mol eq. of ammonia."],"label":"(R)-imazaquin-ammonium","obo_id":"CHEBI:147371","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium 2-[(4R)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]quinoline-3-carboxylate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_147372","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["ammonium 2-[(4S)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]quinoline-3-carboxylate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_147372","description":["An ammonium salt resulting from the formal reaction of the carboxy group of (\u003ci\u003eS\u003c/i\u003e)-imazaquin with 1 mol eq. of ammonia."],"label":"(S)-imazaquin-ammonium","obo_id":"CHEBI:147372","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium 2-[(4S)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]quinoline-3-carboxylate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_147388","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["ammonium 5-methyl-2-[(4R)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]pyridine-3-carboxylate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_147388","description":["An ammonium salt resulting from the formal reaction of the carboxy group of (\u003ci\u003eR\u003c/i\u003e)-imazapic with 1 mol eq. of ammonia."],"label":"(R)-imazapic-ammonium","obo_id":"CHEBI:147388","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium 5-methyl-2-[(4R)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]pyridine-3-carboxylate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_147389","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["ammonium 5-methyl-2-[(4S)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]pyridine-3-carboxylate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_147389","description":["An ammonium salt resulting from the formal reaction of the carboxy group of (\u003ci\u003eS\u003c/i\u003e)-imazapic with 1 mol eq. of ammonia."],"label":"(S)-imazapic-ammonium","obo_id":"CHEBI:147389","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ammonium 5-methyl-2-[(4S)-4-methyl-5-oxo-4-(propan-2-yl)-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-2-yl]pyridine-3-carboxylate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_147402","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["ATS","Thio-Sul","ammo hypo","ammonium hyposulfite","ammonium thiosulfate","ammonium thiosulphate","bisammonium sulfurothioate","diammonium sulfurothioate","diammonium thiosulfate","diammonium thiosulphate","thiosulfuric acid diammonium salt"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_147402","description":["An inorganic ammonium salt composed of ammonium and thiosulfate ions in a 2:1 ratio. It is used in the leaching of gold and silver, as a fertilizer and as a photographic fixing salt."],"label":"ammonium thiosulfate","obo_id":"CHEBI:147402","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["diammonium sulfurothioate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_156543","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["APS","Ammonium peroxydisulfate","Diammonium peroxydisulfate","Diammonium persulfate","Pe